<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tactic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tactic" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Technique
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Technique> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Technique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Technique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A specific method or procedure used by an adversary to achieve a tactic." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Technique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Technique" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ThreatActor
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ThreatActor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ThreatActor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ThreatActor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An individual, group, or organization that conducts malicious cyber operations against CPS environments." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ThreatActor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Threat Actor" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tool
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tool> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tool> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tool> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A software tool used in offensive or defensive cyber operations." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Tool> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tool" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#URL
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#URL> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#URL> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#URL> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A URL reference associated with an ATT&CK entity." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#URL> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "URL" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#VersionPair
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#VersionPair> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#VersionPair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract parent class for pairs associating a device or protocol with a specific firmware or software version." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#VersionPair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Version Pair" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Vulnerability
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Vulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Vulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A known security vulnerability in a software or hardware component." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Vulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vulnerability" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Weakness
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Weakness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Weakness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A software or hardware weakness as defined in the CWE taxonomy." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#Weakness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Weakness" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Root class for all MITRE ATT&CK framework concepts, including tactics, techniques, threat actors, campaigns, and mitigations." .
<https://w3id.org/trace-cps/ontology#ATT&CK> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ATT&CK" .
